# V.32bis at 14400 bit/s -- the top of the Recommendation, and the only
# fixture here that nobody at this end recorded.
#
# A Banksia MyModem 144 (Rockwell) calling out, published with the audio
# by Gough Lui and split into one file per direction; this is the
# answering modem's half, so modec places the call.  Nothing in it came
# out of this code, which is the point: a fixture minted from our own
# recording can pass by agreeing with a mistake we make twice, and this
# one cannot.
#
# The text is the far end's V.42.  132 repetitions of "EC" -- the answer
# detection pattern a V.42 modem sends before it proposes LAPM -- then
# HDLC frames, flag-delimited, byte for byte for the length of the
# recording.  modec speaks MNP and not V.42, so it hands all of it to
# the terminal, which is the right thing to do with bytes it has no
# protocol for.
#
# That is a stronger assertion than the empty reference this fixture
# used to carry, and the empty reference was wrong: the receiver was
# reading the line at a decision error of 0.0015 the whole time, and
# what withheld the bytes was the byte gate's arming rule, which asked
# for half a second of data mode to have passed before it would believe
# a run of descrambled ones.  The one run this far end ever sent
# arrived a tenth of a second early and was refused, and the framer
# then had nothing to arm on for the rest of the call.  A pattern this
# regular, decoded without a single error, is what a working 14400
# receiver looks like; nothing else produces it.
#
# The retrain count matters as much.  Before the
# timing loop was given a tracking gain of its own, this same recording
# connected at 14400 -- the negotiation was never the problem -- and
# then asked for a retrain four seconds later, and again ten seconds
# after that, with the decision error sitting at 0.068 against a margin
# of 0.11.  It now runs at 0.040 and asks for nothing.  Connecting is
# what 'connect:' pins; holding the line is what 'retrains:' pins, and
# only the second of them ever moved.
#
# Re-minted when the caller stopped taking non-AC for AC.  Until then this
# replay went to AA at 3.70 s, inside the answer tone, and "measured" a
# round trip of 60 ms off two reversals that were not the far end's; it
# now goes at 7.92 s on the real AC.  The EC pattern and the LAPM frames
# are byte for byte what they were; the last 88 bytes, which nothing reads
# (decision error through data mode 0.01968 before, 0.01966 after), moved.
source:    recordings/third-party/banksia-mymodem144-answer.wav
seconds:   32.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis
v8:        no
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
tolerance: 0
